    "verified": "2026-10-18",
    "notes": "One current Kv9 pilot, with all eight named treatment centres retained. The official FAQ explicitly accepts dogs and cats; its detailed cancer examples are phrased for dogs, so feline histology and site eligibility require KVS confirmation. Bay of Plenty is location pending and is not represented as an active ninth site. Horse enrollment is outside this catalog. Previous surgery may be accepted if an injectable residual or recurrent tumor remains. Other solid tumors require case-by-case review; no blanket all-cancer or bone-cancer cohort is inferred. The experimental treatment has no guaranteed benefit.",
    "special_requirement": "Pathologist-confirmed cytology or biopsy; accessible tumor approximately 1–5 cm. No concurrent chemotherapy or disallowed immune-modulating medication, but the protocol explicitly permits Apoquel, Cytopoint, Beransa and recent vaccination. Soft tissue sarcoma must not have surface wounds; other tumor types are assessed individually. Residual/recurrent tumors after surgery may qualify if at least 1 × 1 cm remains. Full referral, feline-specific criteria, medication exceptions and site availability require KVS screening."
  },
